From: build <build@local>
Subject: [PATCH 0023] the gates go live

PHASE 2.1 + 2.2 COMPLETION. Applies on merged main (PR #10).

0022 built MarketSnapshot and CarryRisk and wired NEITHER. A gate nothing
consults is documentation.

ONE OBSERVATION, NOT THREE LOOSE READS
main.tick called get_mark, get_funding_bps and get_spot_mark separately and
handed the results to the engine as one instant. The basis is a DIFFERENCE
between two of them, so reading them seconds apart measures the basis plus the
drift between calls. take_snapshot stamps all four with one observation time;
assert_fresh refuses a stale view or a venue clock that disagrees with ours.

A test now counts the reads and asserts ONE each per cycle.

THE PAIR GATE, BEFORE THE FIRST LEG
CarryRisk is consulted inside _open, BEFORE any order goes out. A gate that runs
after one leg has landed is not a gate, it is a post-mortem — and the leg it
would be commenting on is a naked position at carry size.

Until now max_notional_usd was the ONLY size control on this book: the pair
passed through no RiskManager at all. The gate now covers kill switch (unreadable
= engaged), one-pair-only, the cap from shadow.SHADOW_MAX_NOTIONAL_USD, the
margin floor, and one entry per UTC day.

THE DAY ALLOWANCE IS SPENT ONLY ON SUCCESS
record_entry() fires after BOTH legs land. A refused or half-filled pair did not
consume the day, and a test asserts it.

 ~ main.py           take_snapshot + assert_fresh; the view is kept on the
                     engine so the pair gate judges the SAME observation the
                     entry decision used.
 ~ carry_engine.py   pair_risk and snapshot fields; gate consulted in _open;
                     record_entry only after PAIR_LANDED.
 ~ build_bot         attaches CarryRisk with the cap read from shadow — the same
                     constant promotion_gate polices and the engine uses. A test
                     asserts the gate cap and the engine cap are equal.
 ~ Dockerfile        23 modules. market_snapshot and carry_risk entered main's
                     import closure and the image would not have started. The
                     0001 COPY check caught it — the FOURTH time that check has
                     fired on this series.

 + tests/test_carry_live_gates.py   13 tests: one read per field per cycle, a
                     failed or stale view sends no order, an engaged kill switch
                     places nothing, a notional above the gate's cap places
                     nothing even when the ENGINE wants more, and a bare engine
                     in a unit test may still open (the gate is skipped only
                     when absent, never bypassed when present).

VERIFIED: 5,310 passed, 2 skipped (was 5,297). Fixture md5 stable.

STILL NAKED: the book has never touched an exchange. FakeBroker cannot produce a
partial fill, a rate limit, or a maintenance window. 2.3 (testnet drill) and 2.4
(cold start from venue truth) need a host that reaches Bybit.

